From dce8e52c28cf1ea947df7baf4881fce66426c3e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:54:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 36/38] kebab: XNU-003b 'Reboot to bootloader' menu entry

The platform has no way to request fastboot: EFI_RESETREASON_PROTOCOL only
offers Get/Clear, and nothing implements a BCB. BootToBl.efi writes an
Android bootloader control block ('bootonce-bootloader') into the misc
partition, reads it back to prove it stuck, then does a cold reset so ABL
comes up in fastboot.

It is a normal UEFI application, exposed through the config volume as
\EFI\UniXNU\Payloads\BLBOOT.EFI and listed as an 'efi' entry, so UniXNU
itself is unchanged. The menu now reads:

    Hello Payload / Reboot to bootloader / Restart / Power off /
    Return to firmware
